Sending keys: ["cat > /app/output/answer.txt <<'EOF'\n## Statute\n§1(c) - Tax rate for unmarried individuals\n§63(c)(2)(A) - Standard deduction for unmarried individuals ($6,350)\n§151(d)(1) - Personal exemption amount ($2,000)\n§151(d)(3) - Personal exemption phaseout\n§68(b)(1)(C) - Applicable amount for phaseout ($250,000 for unmarried)\n\n## Reasoning\nAlice is unmarried (Bob is her father, not spouse) and not a head of household (no qualifying child mentioned), so §1(c) applies.\n\nStandard deduction: $6,350 under §63(c)(2)(A).\n\nPersonal exemption: $2,000 under §151(d)(1), but subject to phaseout under §151(d)(3).\n\nPhaseout calculation:\n- Alice's AGI: $311,510\n- Applicable amount for unmarried: $250,000 under §68(b)(1)(C)\n- Excess: $311,510 - $250,000 = $61,510\n- Number of $2,500 increments: $61,510 / $2,500 = 24.604\n- Rounded up: 25 increments\n- Applicable percentage: 25 × 2% = 50%\n- Reduced exemption: $2,000 × (1 - 0.50) = $1,000\n\nTaxable income: $311,510 - $6,350 - $1,000 = $304,160\n\nTax calculation under §1(c)(v):\n- Base tax: $79,772\n- Excess over $250,000: $304,160 - $250,000 = $54,160\n- Tax on excess: $54,160 × 39.6% = $21,447.36\n- Total tax: $79,772 + $21,447.36 = $101,219.36\n\nRounded to nearest dollar: $101,219\n\n## Answer\nAnswer: 101219\nEOF\n"] min_timeout_sec: 0.5 max_timeout_sec: 180.0
